WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.127 --> 00:00:05.930
- Yeah, so we got a tip from a friend

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:07.810
that there is vaccines here

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:09.050
in the (speaking foreign language)

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.740
and they're vaccinating people under 50.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:15.030
So we thought to give it a try.

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:16.600
- [Dov Lieber] These young
and middle-aged people

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.060
don't have an appointment but
they've come to this clinic

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:22.500
in Tel Aviv hoping to get
vaccinated against COVID-19.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.763
- I was really nervous to get vaccinated.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:28.370
And we got it.

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:30.220
- While in most countries
around the world,

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:32.960
you have to be part of a
priority group to be vaccinated.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.470
Israeli clinics have been
giving out any remaining doses

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:38.650
to the general public after
the day scheduled appointments

00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:40.940
end for priority patients.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.320
This strategy is one of the
reasons Israel vaccinated

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:46.170
a greater share of its population
than any of the country.

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:48.160
More than 20% in just a few weeks,

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:50.430
way ahead of the U.S.
and European countries

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:53.360
that also have much larger populations.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:55.720
The country hopes to immunize a majority

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:58.400
of its population by early spring.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.490
- Right now what we see is a race.

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:03.470
On one hand, we have the virus spread

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:05.520
spiraling out of control.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:08.420
On the other hand, we have
the vaccination campaign

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:10.480
going very quickly.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:12.370
- [Dov Lieber] Weeks
after the program started

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:15.530
demand was so high, some
clinics had no extra doses left

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:18.856
at the end of the day and
sometimes turned people away.

00:01:18.856 --> 00:01:22.523
(speaking foreign language)

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:32.370
- It's always good to try your chances.

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:35.070
And that's why I hopeful.

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:39.913
But sometimes you get unlucky
but there's always a tomorrow.

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.270
- [Dov Lieber] We wanted to know

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:44.780
how does Israel's program work exactly.

00:01:46.092 --> 00:01:49.759
(speaking foreign language)

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:59.930
Netanyahu announced that
Israel had secured enough doses

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:03.760
of the Pfizer BioNTech shot
to vaccinate everyone over 16

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:05.380
by the end of March.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:08.460
Although this max vaccination
campaign alone is unlikely

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.760
to eradicate the virus, this
timeline sets Israel apart

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.760
as other Western nations
have fallen behind schedule.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:17.290
In the U.S. the vaccination of the elderly

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:18.930
and essential workers alone

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:21.283
is expected to take several more weeks.

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:26.680
One reason Israel has been
able to vaccinate so much

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:29.690
of his population so quickly,
is that it's a relatively

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:31.810
small country with a population

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:34.580
similar to that of New York city.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:37.300
Israel has transformed
stadiums and other venues

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.350
into mass vaccination centers.

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:41.930
Israel also has a technologically advanced

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:45.250
universal healthcare system in
which everyone in the country

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:48.410
is legally required to be
registered unlike the U.S.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:51.560
where there's a patrick of
public and private coverage.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:54.750
Israel's digitized system has
helped streamline the process

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:57.440
for those who have an
appointment, including high risk

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.510
and priority patients over 60.

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:02.130
- Every member set an
appointment in advance

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:04.850
and it's already scheduled
for two appointments.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:08.290
For the first dose and the
second dose 21 days later.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:11.190
Now he comes here in
the exact time and hour

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.760
that we asked him to
come, he uses his card

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:18.760
and pulls out a number and
then someone will take him

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.460
to one of the stations.

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:25.380
And in the station, the nurse
will document everything.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:30.380
His name, his ID and the
number of the bottle.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:33.870
And even in which of the arms

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:35.820
he is going to get the vaccination.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:39.200
And then she will do the
vaccination and he will wait

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:42.763
for about 15 minutes at the
other side of this compound.

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:47.140
- At the start of the
vaccination campaign,

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:50.710
Israel's program ran into big
issues and many vaccine vials

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:52.033
had to be thrown away.

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:55.500
Israel bought 8 million doses from Pfizer,

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.730
paying a premium for early shipments.

00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:00.070
As well as 6 million vaccines for Moderna

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:02.110
and 10 million from AstraZeneca.

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:04.570
When the Pfizer vaccine
first arrived in Israel,

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:06.780
hundreds of doses had to be dumped

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:08.620
due to lower than expected turnout.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:10.980
That's because the BioNTech Pfizer vaccine

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:12.870
must be administered within five days

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:14.730
after leaving the main storage facility

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:17.730
where it must be kept at
ultra cold temperatures

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:21.290
as low as minus 112 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:24.380
After the vaccine dump,
authorities began dividing some

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:26.660
vaccine packages into
smaller shipments for more

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:30.720
isolated areas making for
more efficient distribution.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:33.460
Professor Balicer is the
Chief Innovation Officer

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:36.950
for Clarit, Israel's those
largest healthcare organization.

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:39.410
And he's helped advise
the Israeli government

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:40.830
on his vaccine strategy.

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:44.750
- We have given the full
permission to every delivery point.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:48.780
Once they get to the point
in which the tray of vials

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:52.510
is about to become need
for the destruction

00:04:52.510 --> 00:04:56.700
because of the time limits and
the cold chain requirements,

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:59.780
they are not only allowed,
we want them to go ahead,

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:03.960
find anyone, bring them in
and put a shot in the arm.

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:06.350
So no vaccine would go to waste.

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:08.390
- [Dov Lieber] The vaccines
are now in high demand

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:10.660
and thanks to the latest
shipment of vaccines,

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:13.360
the country set to start
opening up new appointments

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:14.820
to even more people.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:16.990
- I think one of the key
challenges we have right now

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:20.270
is we have no means to get
vaccines to the houses of people

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:23.020
who are bedridden and
cannot leave their home.

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:25.540
What we've tried to do
until now was to vaccinate

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:27.870
their key caregivers.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:29.180
- [Dov Lieber] The
vaccination program comes

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:32.160
at a critical time for
Israel, which early in 2021

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:34.100
had one of the world's
highest infection rates

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.010
and fatalities were on the rise

00:05:36.010 --> 00:05:37.910
as it entered a third lockdown.

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:40.210
There's also the challenge
of vaccine acceptance

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:42.400
with ongoing skepticism over the shots

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.393
and government initiatives in
some parts of the population.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:49.440
Still here in Tel Aviv,
many people have shown up

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:52.520
hoping to get vaccinated
as soon as possible.

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:55.622
- I came here tonight to
try and to get the vaccine

00:05:55.622 --> 00:05:56.455
for the COVID.

00:05:56.455 --> 00:06:01.053
And I want to travel, see
world and starting my life

00:06:01.890 --> 00:06:05.580
like I wanted to and not
to stay out in quarantine

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:07.380
in my house.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:10.463
(soft upbeat music)

